[ar:abhinavflac]
[ti:Lossless]
[al:Lossless]
[by:abhinavflac]
[length:04:08]
[offset:0]

[00:08.87]They told me I wouldn't notice
[00:11.95]what they threw away.
[00:17.66]I noticed.
[00:23.04]Two a.m., the fans are roaring, Arch just broke again
[00:25.65]Flashing ROMs and cold coffee, a cursor for a friend
[00:28.35]Wires in my ears, a FLAC on loop, the one thing I trust
[00:31.13]The feed's a copy of a copy, every edge ground down to dust
[00:33.99]I trained a little oracle to answer "I don't know"
[00:36.55]When the thing you ask it isn't there, it tells you so
[00:39.19]Funny how the machine learned what I never could
[00:41.82]It admits when it's empty, I just say "all good"
[00:44.85]Everything is shrinking into something you can stream
[00:47.43]Summaries of summaries, a smoother kind of dream
[00:49.89]They swear you'll never miss the parts they throw away
[00:52.21]But wired in, I hear the room, I hear the string decay
[00:57.24]Don't compress me
[00:58.85]I'm not 320, I'm not smooth
[01:02.56]Keep the static, keep the tremble
[01:05.21]Keep the parts that sound like truth
[01:07.89]You can shrink me for the server
[01:10.49]You can cut me down to fit
[01:12.67]But I'm lossless, I'm lossless
[01:17.44]I'm keeping every bit
[01:28.82]Moved my own files one night, a robot locked the door
[01:31.59]Mail and Drive and every login, I wasn't me anymore
[01:34.19]Typed my whole heart in a box with a character cap
[01:37.09]It doesn't read intentions, only patterns on a map
[01:39.85]Waited on a verdict from a judge without a face
[01:42.17]Got it all back with no reason, not a sorry, not a trace
[01:44.99]So now I build soft landings for the questions half-begun
[01:47.65]If you're missing the RPM, you still get to run
[01:50.95]I was playing love while someone else was keeping score
[01:55.33]Two a.m., the ceiling, who checks on the strong one anymore?
[02:00.59]Don't compress me
[02:02.13]I'm not 320, I'm not smooth
[02:05.88]Keep the static, keep the tremble
[02:08.53]Keep the parts that sound like truth
[02:11.13]You can shrink me for the server
[02:13.83]You can cut me down to fit
[02:15.97]But I'm lossless, I'm lossless
[02:20.82]I'm keeping every bit, every bit, every bit
[02:24.11]every bit, every bit, every bit
[02:26.07]I'm keeping every bit, every bit
[02:28.73]every bit, every bit, every bit
[02:37.06]Minus one.
[02:43.50]Ran my life through DBSCAN, it filed me under noise
[02:48.05]Thought a hundred times about a chair, zero times for you
[02:53.39]Give it freely, feel it fully, don't swallow the sound
[02:58.87]I'm allowed to be the one somebody gives to now
[03:03.90]Don't compress me
[03:05.45]I'm not background, I'm not smooth
[03:09.18]Keep the crackle, keep the trembling
[03:11.81]Keep the parts that sound like truth
[03:14.49]Buy the chair, get the monitor, say it when it hurts a bit
[03:19.75]You can shrink me for the server
[03:22.40]You can cut me down to fit
[03:24.53]But I'm lossless, I'm lossless
[03:29.33]I'm keeping every bit
[03:34.68]I'm keeping every bit
[03:43.02]Bit-perfect.
[03:46.42]Life is good.
[03:49.44]Really, this time.
